WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.334
-The saga of Tucker Carlson's
messy and abrupt exit

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.200
from Fox News
is still ongoing,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.300
with yet more revelations
and speculation

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.133
about what exactly
led to his ouster.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:13.400
The story is yet another example
of just how weak and fractured

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.667
the already unpopular
MAGA movement has become.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.901
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.834
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:25.434
After his abrupt and mysterious
dismissal from Fox News,

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.167
Tucker Carlson posted
what I guess was

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.601
some sort of proof-of-life video
on Twitter last night...

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:30.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.234
...filmed from what I can
only assume is a secret lair

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.601
at the base of a volcano

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:38.234
or a fake doctor's office
from a low-budget porno.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.234
Seriously, why are you
zooming in from your sauna?

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:45.567
That place looks like
the Unabomber's hideout

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:48.334
if he updated it
and put it on Airbnb.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:49.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.934
I also love the carefully
planted details

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:53.534
in the background,
like the globe.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:57.167
Ooh! Ooh! A globe on a shelf!

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.968
It's like we're supposed
to think to ourselves,

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.434
"This mother[Bleep] is worldly!"

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:02.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.868
Also, what is it with
these right-wing weirdos

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.667
filming incredibly
close-up videos

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.334
from their phony-looking
home studios?

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.701
Trump does the same thing now
with his stupid campaign videos.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.400
You know, his Zach Galifianakis
rip-off between two flags.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:20.467
Now, Tucker never addressed
his ouster from Fox,

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:23.000
and most of what he said in the
video is utterly meaningless.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.133
But he did end
on a somewhat unnerving note.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.501
-When honest people
say what's true,

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.767
calmly and
without embarrassment,

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.834
they become powerful.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.467
At the same time, the liars

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.167
who've been trying
to silence them

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.501
shrink and they become weaker.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.400
That's the iron law
of the universe.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.334
True things prevail.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.934
Where can you still find
Americans saying true things?

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:48.601
There aren't many places left,
but there are some.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:49.934
And that's enough.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.634
As long as you
can hear the words,

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:54.234
there is hope.
See you soon.

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:55.968
-I'm impressed by
the confidence of a man

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.834
who went from filming
a top-rated TV show

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.934
in a flashy high-budget studio
to posting Twitter videos

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.167
from what I can only assume is

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.067
an episode
of "Tiny House Nation."

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.667
He looks like he's auditioning
to be the new chief

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.801
on "Where in the World
Is Carmen Sandiego?"

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.934
[ Laughter ]
"Hello, gumshoes.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.968
Can you spot Carmen Sandiego
in this peaceful protest?"

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.334
Let's zoom in. There she is."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:22.000
"Good work, gumshoes."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.033
Also, it's very --
it's very chilling

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.901
when a figure
as nefarious as Tucker

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.901
ends a self-taped video
from an undisclosed location

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:32.834
with the words "See you soon"
and then just disappears.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.567
He should have pointed
to the globe when he said that.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:38.834
"See you soon, Jakarta."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.000
That's how a jilted husband
ends a voicemail

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.634
in a Lifetime movie.
Next thing you know,

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.634
he's on your balcony
in a thunderstorm,

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.167
staring at you
through your window.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.100
"Hello, darling, it's me.
I told you I'd see you soon.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.000
[ Laughing maniacally ]

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.100
But that's ridiculous.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.734
This isn't actually
a Lifetime movie.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.968
Tucker's never actually
started out his show

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:01.367
with some sinister
hypothetical like that.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.434
-But, first tonight,

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:03.601
what if
your next-door neighbor

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.634
suddenly went dangerously insane

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.367
and started holding people
hostage in his house?

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.667
Would you consider
that threatening?

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.234
Would you even notice it?

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.901
-Jesus!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:18.167
That's how you start the show?!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.534
How about a little ramp-up,
a couple jokes, or something?

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.167
He might as well have said,
"Good evening.

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.834
Look out behind you.
He's got a knife!"

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.534
Why is he talking about a
hypothetical next-door neighbor

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:29.968
who suddenly goes insane?

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:32.334
He sounds like he's pitching
a dark reboot of "Seinfeld"

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:35.200
called "Breaking Kramer."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.434
Of course, the difference is,

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.501
Kramer is not
the one who knocks.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.400
-Hey.
-Hey.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.934
So, Sal wrote that
"not the one who knocks" joke.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.133
And I read it,
and I didn't quite get it.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:49.567
And he goes,
"You can cut it if you want."

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.667
And I'm like, "If I cut it,
how will you learn your lesson?"

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.767
But...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.868
By the way, if you're
curious what --

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:10.667
It was the absence of a laugh.
Did you notice that?

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.667
By the way, if you're curious

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.133
what Tucker
was actually talking about

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.534
in that deranged hypothetical,
he was talking about Canada.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:20.901
I swear I'm not making that up.
Here, watch.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:22.734
-Those are not
theoretical questions.

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:24.467
Something very much like that
just happened

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:27.133
in our national neighborhood.
Canada...

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.133
-It's amazing that
the list of Tucker Carlson's

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.901
imagined enemies now includes
the entire nation of Canada.

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:35.501
And somehow that's not even
the weirdest thing on it.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.000
Anyway, Tucker posted
this weird little video

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.567
to, I guess, prove
that he still exists

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:42.734
after the network he worked for

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.300
essentially
disappeared him overnight.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.801
So far, there's been
a lot of speculation

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.367
over what exactly
led to his exit,

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:48.601
but nothing concrete yet.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.267
On the one hand,
the "L.A. Times" reported

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.334
that Tucker was pushed out
by Rupert Murdoch himself

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.133
and that Carlson's exit
is related

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:57.000
to a discrimination lawsuit
filed by Abby Grossberg,

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.901
a producer fired
by the network last month.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.667
Meanwhile,
the "Wall Street Journal"

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.167
reported that Tucker Carlson's
vulgar, offensive messages

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.467
about his colleagues helped
seal his fate at Fox News.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:08.734
And then "Vanity Fair" reported
yet another, stranger theory

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:10.567
that Tucker Carlson's
prayer talk

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:12.467
may have led
to his Fox News ouster,

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:15.267
with one source saying,
"That stuff freaks Rupert out."

00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:16.767
And it wouldn't surprise me.

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.701
Rupert Murdoch definitely
seems like the kind of guy who,

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:20.701
even if he did go to church,
would play hardball

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.400
when the collection basket
comes around.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.033
"I'm not giving you [Bleep]
a bloody cent

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.934
unless I get
VIP access to Heaven."

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.968
"Look, we can't we can't --

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.901
We can't guarantee VIP access.

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:34.567
We can tell Saint Peter
to expedite the entry process."

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.467
"Alright, alright,
here's a dollar.

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.200
Hold on,
I'm taking out 85 cents.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.501
Don't move the basket,
ya [Bleep]."

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:44.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.868
By the way, it also wouldn't
surprise me

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:47.734
if, when it comes to a guy
like Tucker Carlson,

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:50.334
there was, you know,
more than one reason

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:51.601
for getting [Bleep] canned.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:54.367
Like, when they finally
nabbed Jeffrey Dahmer,

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.267
they weren't like,
"This is just for the last one."

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.868
And sure enough, last night,

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:00.834
"The New York Times"
reported new information

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:02.767
that Fox News board members
had discovered

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:05.267
even more vulgar text messages
that were so bad

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:07.868
they felt they needed
to sever ties with Tucker ASAP.

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:10.167
-Fox recently settled
a defamation lawsuit

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:13.634
with Dominion Voting Systems
for nearly $800 million

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.868
that alleged the network
repeatedly lied

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:18.133
about debunked
election-fraud claims.

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:20.534
Private texts and e-mails
from Carlson

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:23.901
emerged during the lawsuit,
including redacted messages

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:25.634
about Fox News executives.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:28.868
-"The New York Times" reports
Carlson's redacted text messages

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.667
were even worse than ones

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:32.734
which were revealed
in those court filings.

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:35.901
And there was one message
that was particularly offensive,

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:38.868
which added to the concern
at the top of the company.

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.901
-Wow.
So, Fox put up with his racism,

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:43.334
bigotry, harassment, and
conspiracy theories for years.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.434
But then they saw
this one text message

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:48.767
and said, "We got to get this
guy the [Bleep] outta here."

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:50.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:51.834
I mean, what did
that text message say?

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:53.400
"I'll tell you what --
that Joe Biden

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.400
makes some good points"?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.133
If you zoom out from
the specifics of the Tucker saga

00:06:58.133 --> 00:06:59.734
for a second,
there's a bigger story here.

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.801
The drama and infighting
that's now consumed the GOP,

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:04.567
Fox News, and the MAGA movement
is due in large part

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.133
to the fact that
their political project

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:08.367
has been an abject failure.
People don't want it.

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:10.400
They've lost in election
after election after election,

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.834
and their tactics
have caught up to them.

00:07:11.834 --> 00:07:13.667
That's why they're trying
to turn the page

00:07:13.667 --> 00:07:16.000
and pivot to guys
like Ron DeSantis.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.200
But much like the rest
of the MAGA crowd,

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.067
DeSantis is so weird
and off-putting,

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:22.868
he's falling behind
in the polls.

00:07:22.868 --> 00:07:25.067
Even his speaking cadence
is incredibly weird.

00:07:25.067 --> 00:07:27.601
Just listen to him try
to deliver a normal speech.

00:07:27.601 --> 00:07:30.634
-Republicans need to shake
the culture of losing

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:33.501
that has developed
in recent years.

00:07:33.501 --> 00:07:36.367
The time for excuses is over.

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:37.801
-What is up with this dude?

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:40.334
He sounds like he's starring
in a middle-school production

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:42.534
of "Joseph and the Amazing
Technicolor Dreamcoat."

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:45.100
[ Stiffly ] Hello,
my name is Joseph,

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.100
and this is
my amazing new Dreamcoat.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:53.167
It's just regular brown because
Technicolor has a gay agenda."

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.834 --> 00:07:57.267
DeSantis is so awkward
and uncharismatic,

00:07:57.267 --> 00:08:01.234
he's somehow lagging behind an
even more off-putting weirdo --

00:08:01.234 --> 00:08:03.501
the GOP front-runner/
current criminal defendant,

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:07.033
Donald Trump, who, in addition
to being under indictment,

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:09.267
Trump is also, as we've
documented many times before,

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:10.868
a weird man.
For example,

00:08:10.868 --> 00:08:12.567
he was campaigning
recently in Florida,

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:14.067
where he stopped
at a pizza place

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:16.133
and offered his fans some pizza

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.334
in typically weird
Trump fashion.

00:08:18.334 --> 00:08:20.534
-[ Chanting ] Trump! Trump!
Trump! Trump!

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:24.734
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:27.801
-Jesus Christ.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:27.801 --> 00:08:30.467
In 40 years,
the Republican Party

00:08:30.467 --> 00:08:33.367
has gone from, "Mr. Gorbachev,
tear down this wall,"

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:36.067
to, "Does anyone want
a piece I've eaten?"

00:08:36.067 --> 00:08:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.133 --> 00:08:45.434
No wonder Tucker Carlson is
hiding in a child's playhouse.

00:08:45.434 --> 00:08:47.734
"Does anyone want
a piece I've eaten?"

00:08:47.734 --> 00:08:50.000
Do you mean like, you'll
chew it up, digest it,

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.100
and then baby-bird it
into their mouths?

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.467
"Would anyone like
a soggy piece of pizza?

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.701
It's covered --
covered in my saliva

00:08:57.701 --> 00:09:00.434
and has already been
premasticated by yours truly.

00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:03.501
Masticated.
We love masticated, don't we?

00:09:03.501 --> 00:09:05.601
It means "chewed,"
but it's a tricky word

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:08.133
because it sounds like
the other one.

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:10.033
Masticated -- it sound --

00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:11.834
You know the one
I'm talking about, right?

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:14.734
The M-word.
We call it the M-word

00:09:14.734 --> 00:09:17.567
because we don't like to say it
and we don't like to do it,

00:09:17.567 --> 00:09:19.667
because if we do it,
we go blind."

00:09:19.667 --> 00:09:23.267
"And our you-know-whats,
they..."

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:25.701
-Shrink and they become weaker.

00:09:25.701 --> 00:09:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.234
"My God, what is happening?

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:33.501
Hey!"

00:09:33.501 --> 00:09:36.634
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.934 --> 00:09:43.968
That's our new -- I mean,
our new slang

00:09:43.968 --> 00:09:46.133
for a video clip
that doesn't work is Kramered.

00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:49.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:51.667
Just like
the Dominion settlement

00:09:51.667 --> 00:09:55.200
or the elections of 2018,
2020, and 2022,

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.300
the saga of Tucker Carlson's
fall from grace

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.901
is yet another example
of what happens

00:09:58.901 --> 00:10:01.133
when the right-wing echo chamber
collides with reality.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:03.667
It's a movement led by cruel,
malicious bullies

00:10:03.667 --> 00:10:05.367
who think they're untouchable

00:10:05.367 --> 00:10:06.801
and who lie to their audience
with contempt.

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.234
And now it's
catching up to them.

00:10:08.234 --> 00:10:09.834
Every time Trump
and the MAGA crowd

00:10:09.834 --> 00:10:11.367
think they've achieved peace
within the Republican Party,

00:10:11.367 --> 00:10:13.033
it turns out it's...

00:10:14.467 --> 00:10:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.334 --> 00:10:18.300
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.968
[ Theme music plays ]

00:10:19.968 --> 00:10:21.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

